From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ai_re <ai_re@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:10:36 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] board: Celestica CS8210-32X on the Alpine V3 target

U-Boot additions to the board's Linux DTS (arch/arm/dts/alpine-v3-cs8210.dts,
copied in at build time from the Linux board tree, not part of this patch),
in alpine-v3-cs8210-u-boot.dtsi:
- the seven internal AHCI functions without the SSD (00:08-00:0a and
  00:0c-00:0f) disabled for U-Boot only: stage3 gives SATA one SerDes lane
  and the SSD is on 00:0b.0 port 3;
- the boot flash SSI at 25 MHz (U-Boot caps transfers at the controller's
  value, 500 kHz when absent) and aliases/spi0 = that SSI.

alpine_v3_cs8210_defconfig: TEXT_BASE 0x08000000 (the vendor loadaddr),
console on UART0 (500 MHz, 32-bit registers) plus a debug UART that skips
init; standard boot (extlinux, boot.scr) over PCI ECAM -> AHCI -> SCSI with
ext4/FAT, booti, sysboot, bootmenu + env import (what the NixOS boot.scr
uses); I2C with the pca954x muxes; the boot flash read-only (0019 +
the 4-byte reads, no lock/SFDP/soft-reset code, no write window); reset
through PSCI SYSTEM_RESET (the V3 monitor is PSCI v0.2); no network, no
MMC, no EFI; env nowhere.

Scope: cs8210.
---
 arch/arm/dts/alpine-v3-cs8210-u-boot.dtsi | 63 +++++++++++++++++
 configs/alpine_v3_cs8210_defconfig        | 82 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 145 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/dts/alpine-v3-cs8210-u-boot.dtsi
 create mode 100644 configs/alpine_v3_cs8210_defconfig

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/alpine-v3-cs8210-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/alpine-v3-cs8210-u-boot.dtsi
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..3df776a3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/alpine-v3-cs8210-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0+
+/*
+ * U-Boot additions for the Celestica CS8210-32X. The board DTS itself
+ * (alpine-v3-cs8210.dts) is the Linux one, copied in at build time; it
+ * already carries the four DRAM banks and the firmware ranges
+ * (/reserved-memory) that al-boot reports.
+ */
+
+#include "alpine-v3-u-boot.dtsi"
+
+/*
+ * Internal PCIe (ECAM, bus 0): eight AHCI functions 00:08.0..00:0f.0, but
+ * stage3 gives SATA one SerDes lane (main 15) and the SSD hangs off port 3
+ * of 00:0b.0 (Linux: ata16 = controller 3, port 3; the vendor U-Boot:
+ * "SCSI controller: 3"). The other seven only add 4 x 200 ms of link
+ * timeouts each, so U-Boot leaves them alone (Linux still sees all eight).
+ */
+&{/soc/pcie@fbd00000} {
+	sata@8,0 {
+		reg = <0x4000 0 0 0 0>;
+		status = "disabled";
+	};
+	sata@9,0 {
+		reg = <0x4800 0 0 0 0>;
+		status = "disabled";
+	};
+	sata@a,0 {
+		reg = <0x5000 0 0 0 0>;
+		status = "disabled";
+	};
+	sata@c,0 {
+		reg = <0x6000 0 0 0 0>;
+		status = "disabled";
+	};
+	sata@d,0 {
+		reg = <0x6800 0 0 0 0>;
+		status = "disabled";
+	};
+	sata@e,0 {
+		reg = <0x7000 0 0 0 0>;
+		status = "disabled";
+	};
+	sata@f,0 {
+		reg = <0x7800 0 0 0 0>;
+		status = "disabled";
+	};
+};
+
+/*
+ * Boot flash SSI. U-Boot's DW SSI caps every transfer at the controller's
+ * own spi-max-frequency (500 kHz when absent); read at the flash's 25 MHz,
+ * as Linux and the vendor U-Boot do. seq 0 = this SSI, so "sf probe 0:0" is
+ * the boot flash whatever the probe order.
+ */
+&spi0 {
+	spi-max-frequency = <25000000>;
+};
+
+/ {
+	aliases {
+		spi0 = &spi0;
+	};
+};
diff --git a/configs/alpine_v3_cs8210_defconfig b/configs/alpine_v3_cs8210_defconfig
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..5290bdcc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/configs/alpine_v3_cs8210_defconfig
@@ -0,0 +1,82 @@
